WEBVTT

03:08.982 --> 03:10.400
We're close.

03:37.052 --> 03:38.804
Ah! Ah...

03:41.390 --> 03:42.474
Aargh!

03:48.271 --> 03:49.898
I'll find a rock.

03:51.942 --> 03:52.985
Ah...

04:07.457 --> 04:09.042
It can't end like this...

04:40.657 --> 04:41.908
It's okay.

04:42.659 --> 04:44.036
Come here.

04:48.999 --> 04:50.542
There's nothing.

04:55.881 --> 04:57.507
Nothing to be done.

05:16.401 --> 05:18.070
Just turn away.

05:18.403 --> 05:19.738
Be still.

05:26.369 --> 05:28.080
I said turn away!

05:46.306 --> 05:47.473
Aaaargh!

08:10.158 --> 08:16.456
♪ Oft in the stilly night ♪

08:16.790 --> 08:23.755
♪ Ere slumber's chain
has bound me ♪

08:25.340 --> 08:31.053
♪ Fond memory
brings the light ♪

08:31.054 --> 08:37.727
♪ Of other days around me ♪

08:40.355 --> 08:43.232
♪ The smiles, the tears ♪

08:43.233 --> 08:45.777
♪ Of boyhood's years ♪

08:46.611 --> 08:51.283
♪ The words of love
then spoken ♪

08:53.451 --> 08:56.121
♪ The eyes that shone ♪

08:56.454 --> 08:59.791
♪ Now dimm'd and gone ♪

09:00.750 --> 09:06.172
♪ The cheerful hearts
now broken ♪

09:51.509 --> 09:53.011
Why'd you shoot it?

09:53.553 --> 09:55.013
They're pests.

09:55.305 --> 09:58.266
They jump up on the cars
and make shit of the paintwork.

09:59.351 --> 10:01.102
Couldn't just shoo it away, huh?

10:01.811 --> 10:03.104
Goats are stubborn.

10:04.647 --> 10:06.149
Spray it with a hose?

10:08.568 --> 10:09.569
No.

10:17.535 --> 10:18.827
I'm telling you now, Fergal,

10:18.828 --> 10:20.496
I'm not dragging that
into the woods.

10:20.497 --> 10:21.373
Shut up.

10:21.706 --> 10:23.500
Fado, fado...

10:23.958 --> 10:27.044
Long, long ago,
deep in the woods,

10:27.045 --> 10:29.339
there was a small stone hut.

10:29.839 --> 10:32.174
And inside the stone hut,

10:32.175 --> 10:35.345
there lived an old Cailleach...

10:36.554 --> 10:37.931
A witch.

10:38.890 --> 10:40.809
Preying upon the lost,

10:40.975 --> 10:44.228
the evil old crone would first
put the doomed travellers

10:44.229 --> 10:45.772
under her spell,

10:46.064 --> 10:50.276
leaving them as dazzled
and vulnerable as lamplit game.

10:52.320 --> 10:55.531
The witch would then shackle
her stunned prey

10:55.532 --> 10:58.158
before taking
the lost travellers

10:58.159 --> 11:00.578
on a tour of the underworld.

11:01.496 --> 11:03.163
And sometimes,

11:03.164 --> 11:06.917
a hand or a claw
would reach out from the dark

11:06.918 --> 11:10.922
and tear a piece from those
at the end of her chain.

11:11.631 --> 11:13.216
Pluck out an eye.

11:13.925 --> 11:15.343
Peel off an ear.

11:16.886 --> 11:18.262
And sometimes,

11:18.263 --> 11:20.848
they took something
from a little boy

11:20.849 --> 11:24.602
that was more valuable to him
than his eyes or ears.

11:25.770 --> 11:30.065
Any guesses which part of you
that might be?

11:31.484 --> 11:33.486
- These your kids?
- No.

11:35.822 --> 11:37.198
Go find your parents.

11:39.159 --> 11:41.369
And don't talk
to strangers again.

11:44.289 --> 11:47.792
There are worse things
than strangers out there, Yank.

11:52.297 --> 11:53.923
Did we wake you?

11:54.048 --> 11:55.675
Uh, Mr Cob, my apologies.

11:56.009 --> 11:58.385
I was on the phone and I thought
Alby was manning...

11:58.386 --> 12:00.762
Don't apologise to me,
you maneen.

12:00.763 --> 12:02.474
Apologise to the guest!

12:02.932 --> 12:04.099
My apologies.

12:04.100 --> 12:05.684
Why don't you mind
your own business?

12:05.685 --> 12:06.769
It is my business.

12:07.896 --> 12:09.481
I'm the owner.

12:11.232 --> 12:13.400
Bauman. I have a reservation.

12:13.401 --> 12:17.654
If you could just sign...
Ah! Mr Bauman.

12:17.655 --> 12:20.074
Mr Ohm Bauman,
Pullman City, Washington.

12:20.200 --> 12:22.743
With us for a week. Welcome.

12:22.744 --> 12:24.412
Lock it up.

12:26.664 --> 12:28.458
Alby's dragging it out
into the woods.

12:30.126 --> 12:33.004
Dining room is down
this corridor here.

12:33.463 --> 12:35.840
Breakfast in the morning
from seven to ten.

12:36.007 --> 12:38.509
Halloween party tomorrow night
with live music,

12:38.510 --> 12:40.302
cocktails, costumes...

12:40.303 --> 12:41.679
Should be a bit of craic.

12:41.888 --> 12:44.556
Oh, um, craic is a word we use

12:44.557 --> 12:46.350
to describe a fun time
here in Ireland.

12:46.351 --> 12:47.893
Yeah, can I get a room
as far away

12:47.894 --> 12:50.021
from the 'craic' as possible?

12:50.355 --> 12:52.690
- I've work to do.
- What do you do?

12:52.899 --> 12:54.067
Writer.

12:55.902 --> 12:57.195
Well...

12:58.321 --> 12:59.780
you shouldn't hear a thing.

12:59.781 --> 13:00.782
Thank you.

13:02.534 --> 13:05.078
Wait... Bauman.

13:05.245 --> 13:07.205
Ah, I know that name.

13:08.039 --> 13:10.833
I think my son
is a fan of yours!

13:11.834 --> 13:13.336
A celebrity.

13:14.128 --> 13:15.420
Well, if there's anything
we can do

13:15.421 --> 13:17.256
to make your stay
more enjoyable,

13:17.257 --> 13:19.676
please dial '0' and let us know.

13:19.801 --> 13:21.010
All right.

13:21.427 --> 13:23.595
Oh, maybe I could bring in
my son's book

13:23.596 --> 13:24.889
and you could sign it for him?

13:25.890 --> 13:26.975
No.

13:37.819 --> 13:39.612
There's nothing
getting through that.

13:40.029 --> 13:41.573
That's built to last.

13:53.126 --> 13:55.211
Oh, for fuck's sake.

13:55.420 --> 13:56.963
Are you lost?

13:57.297 --> 13:58.881
What does it look like?

13:59.090 --> 14:02.426
Well, with that attitude,
it looks like you can stay lost.

14:02.427 --> 14:04.761
Okay, sorry, I'm just...
I can't find my room.

14:04.762 --> 14:08.016
It should be right here,
but it's not.

14:08.850 --> 14:11.185
- Oh, yeah. It's this way.
- Thank you.

14:12.353 --> 14:14.772
- First time in Ireland?
- Yeah.

14:15.148 --> 14:16.858
Are you having a nice time?

14:17.358 --> 14:18.401
Yeah.

14:19.527 --> 14:21.112
This is you.

14:21.529 --> 14:22.655
Thank you.

14:22.905 --> 14:24.240
Enjoy your stay.

14:24.782 --> 14:27.201
Thanks. Oh, hey...

14:27.910 --> 14:30.705
Sorry, would you happen to know

14:31.914 --> 14:35.001
with the Big Redwood is?

16:09.303 --> 16:10.972
- Who are those?
- Jesus...

16:14.016 --> 16:15.435
Oh, uh...

16:16.227 --> 16:17.645
My folks.

16:19.272 --> 16:20.690
Sorry for your loss.

16:22.817 --> 16:24.359
You want a drink?

16:24.360 --> 16:27.113
I think I may need something
stronger than milk.

16:31.617 --> 16:33.161
Nothing stronger than that.

16:35.455 --> 16:37.665
- Moonshine?
- Poitín.

16:38.124 --> 16:39.584
Uisce beatha.

16:39.917 --> 16:41.294
Water of life.

16:43.796 --> 16:46.090
Whoo. Yeah, that's moonshine.

16:47.008 --> 16:48.842
If you want something
to defeat the demons,

16:48.843 --> 16:50.553
and not just be
running from them.

16:51.095 --> 16:52.555
Magic mushrooms.

16:54.265 --> 16:55.725
Psilocybin.

16:56.309 --> 16:57.685
It's all natural.

16:58.686 --> 17:01.647
I pick, dry, and grind
the mushrooms myself.

17:02.732 --> 17:04.525
And I like it with goat's milk.

17:06.152 --> 17:07.819
What are you gonna do with it?

17:07.820 --> 17:09.905
- I'll bury her.
- Hm.

17:09.906 --> 17:12.283
Do you know why they climb
on the cars?

17:14.702 --> 17:17.537
Goats like to graze
on the mushrooms as well.

17:17.538 --> 17:18.955
And when they're coming up,

17:18.956 --> 17:23.044
they go looking for reflective
surfaces, 'cause...

17:24.128 --> 17:27.507
staring into your own eyes
on mushrooms

17:28.007 --> 17:29.759
deepens the trip.

17:30.968 --> 17:32.178
But...

17:32.929 --> 17:34.514
it can be dangerous.

17:34.806 --> 17:37.600
Especially if there's an asshole
with a crossbow nearby.

17:38.184 --> 17:39.684
Don't get me started.

17:39.685 --> 17:42.146
I've nearly come to blows
with him over it.

17:42.605 --> 17:43.815
Thanks for the drink.

17:45.983 --> 17:47.943
Don't go climbing up
on any cars.

17:47.944 --> 17:50.112
I won't!

18:06.838 --> 18:11.591
The boy's skull is the only hard
object for, like, miles.

18:11.592 --> 18:14.303
So, the conquistador

18:14.762 --> 18:17.932
hits the boy with the bottle,
killing him,

18:18.140 --> 18:21.143
but the bottle
still doesn't break.

18:22.353 --> 18:26.649
In the end, he wanders out
into the desert to die.

18:34.198 --> 18:36.534
- Why would you write this?
- What do you mean?

18:36.742 --> 18:39.203
I mean, it's so bleak.

18:39.328 --> 18:41.956
Well, you know, it's meant
to be challenging.

18:42.665 --> 18:46.544
Well, I won't be reading it.
Not if that's how it ends.

18:47.670 --> 18:49.296
Well, you know,
a few of my novels

18:49.297 --> 18:50.755
have been turned
into bad movies,

18:50.756 --> 18:53.216
and when they make
the movie for you,

18:53.217 --> 18:55.177
you tag on a happy ending.

18:55.511 --> 18:57.722
Okay, well, they'd better.

18:59.682 --> 19:01.809
You remind me of my mom.

19:02.935 --> 19:05.896
Your mum? How old
do you think I am?

19:05.897 --> 19:08.107
Well, when she was young,
you know.

19:10.818 --> 19:12.695
Yeah, just in the way she...

19:15.865 --> 19:17.867
Hm. She looks happy.

19:17.992 --> 19:19.952
My dad took that.

19:20.286 --> 19:21.995
You know, they came here
for their honeymoon.

19:21.996 --> 19:23.539
Always wanted to come back.

19:23.664 --> 19:25.081
- Oh yeah?
- Yeah.

19:25.082 --> 19:26.541
Why didn't they?

19:26.542 --> 19:28.961
Oh, she died a few years
after that.

19:30.129 --> 19:32.214
- She was very young.
- Mm.

19:32.381 --> 19:34.425
- How did she die?
- Murdered.

19:35.343 --> 19:38.471
Shot in the face
as she came home from work.

19:40.014 --> 19:41.932
Did they catch the person
that shot her?

19:41.933 --> 19:44.018
Nah, he's too young
to be punished.

19:44.268 --> 19:46.020
Should have fucking hanged him.

19:48.105 --> 19:49.607
And your dad?

19:50.149 --> 19:53.610
Oh, well, he...
turned into a monster

19:53.611 --> 19:55.529
and drank himself
to an early grave.

19:58.324 --> 20:01.409
You know, I've had
their ashes for years

20:01.410 --> 20:03.078
and never knew
what to do with them.

20:03.079 --> 20:05.247
I knew they were happy
here, so...

20:06.165 --> 20:09.794
Hey, I noticed the honeymoon
suite, it's closed.

20:10.544 --> 20:12.463
I wonder if that's the room
they stayed in.

20:12.797 --> 20:15.341
That has been closed
a long time.

20:15.800 --> 20:17.218
Do you know why?

20:17.426 --> 20:21.055
Because no couple in their right
mind would honeymoon here?

20:21.472 --> 20:22.974
It's haunted.

20:24.183 --> 20:26.560
- Oh.
- By a witch.

20:27.395 --> 20:30.690
Mr Cob says they managed to lock
her in there years ago.

20:31.357 --> 20:35.276
I tried to convince Mal
to sneak the key off Mr Cob

20:35.277 --> 20:36.862
so I could have a look up there,

20:37.238 --> 20:39.865
but... he wouldn't go for it.

20:40.282 --> 20:44.202
I have never known a man to be
so afraid of his father-in-law.

20:44.203 --> 20:45.912
Why do you want to go up there
so bad?

20:45.913 --> 20:47.872
To see if there really is
a witch up there.

20:47.873 --> 20:48.957
What if there is?

20:48.958 --> 20:50.417
I mean, aren't you
afraid she'll,

20:50.418 --> 20:51.752
uh, 'get you'?

20:57.258 --> 21:00.176
- I'd bring some chalk.
- Chalk?

21:00.177 --> 21:02.762
If you ever find yourself
being chased by a witch,

21:02.763 --> 21:04.889
draw a circle around you.
Keep you safe.

21:04.890 --> 21:06.850
If I ever think I'm being chased
by a witch,

21:06.851 --> 21:10.103
I will look for a psychiatrist,
not a piece of chalk.

21:11.689 --> 21:13.481
Oh, perfect. Alby...

21:13.482 --> 21:15.316
Tell Ohm here about
your encounter

21:15.317 --> 21:16.736
with the witch upstairs.

21:19.155 --> 21:20.531
Well, um...

21:38.424 --> 21:39.675
Hello?

22:36.816 --> 22:38.150
And that's what happened.

22:39.401 --> 22:40.736
Hokum.

22:42.071 --> 22:43.614
Don't worry, Alby.

22:43.823 --> 22:44.949
I believe you.

22:46.367 --> 22:48.536
Fiona?
Delivery to sign for.

22:51.205 --> 22:52.498
Back in a sec.

22:55.876 --> 22:57.962
Are you enjoying your stay,
Mr Bauman?

22:59.171 --> 23:00.464
Yeah, I guess.

23:01.966 --> 23:05.136
When I saw the name, I didn't
think it would actually be you.

23:05.678 --> 23:07.304
Uh, what are you doing here?

23:08.639 --> 23:10.099
Who knows?

23:11.183 --> 23:13.560
I don't mean to bother you,
but I wanted to tell you

23:13.561 --> 23:15.146
how much your books
have meant to me.

23:15.479 --> 23:17.480
I really relate
to your characters.

23:17.481 --> 23:18.731
Well, that's troubling,

23:18.732 --> 23:20.900
seeing as those pages
are populated

23:20.901 --> 23:24.572
by deeply disturbed,
desperate people.

23:25.656 --> 23:28.534
Oh, is that what you use to keep
track of all your ideas?

23:29.785 --> 23:31.161
It is, yeah.

23:31.162 --> 23:34.957
And in fact, I just had one
speaking with you.

23:38.085 --> 23:40.003
Idea for a character,

23:40.004 --> 23:43.465
uh, oblivious charisma vacuum.

23:44.383 --> 23:48.762
Is completely incapable
of reading a room.

23:49.722 --> 23:50.973
Ah...

23:51.974 --> 23:54.601
Is it true, I read
that you're finally writing

23:54.602 --> 23:56.227
the end of the Conquistador
trilogy?

23:56.228 --> 23:57.813
How fuck do I know
what you read?

23:58.063 --> 24:00.608
No, I mean, is it true you're
finally writing the ending?

24:01.525 --> 24:04.111
I'm starting to think
it's gonna be open-ended.

24:04.486 --> 24:06.572
And are you happy
with how it's going?

24:08.532 --> 24:09.950
I'm a writer too.

24:10.409 --> 24:13.078
And some nights it's hard
to face that blank page.

24:16.081 --> 24:17.208
Yeah.

24:18.334 --> 24:20.920
So that's a Halloween costume
you're wearing?

24:22.129 --> 24:23.880
Oh, uh, no.

24:23.881 --> 24:25.673
I-I just work here
to pay the bills.

24:25.674 --> 24:29.511
Oh. Oh, okay. So you're not
a writer, you're a bellboy.

24:30.763 --> 24:34.182
No, I am a writer. I just
don't get paid for it yet.

24:34.183 --> 24:35.725
- Ah.
- You know, it can be hard

24:35.726 --> 24:38.561
to get publishers or agents
or anybody to read anything.

24:38.562 --> 24:39.813
Sure.

24:41.315 --> 24:43.900
And actually, um, I've got
a manuscript in my locker.

24:43.901 --> 24:45.526
Do you mind if I ask you
to take a look at it?

24:45.527 --> 24:46.528
Nope.

24:46.862 --> 24:48.738
Why not?

24:48.739 --> 24:50.657
Ah! Jesus...

24:50.658 --> 24:52.033
You need thicker skin than that

24:52.034 --> 24:53.827
if you wanna make it
as a writer.

24:58.791 --> 25:00.167
What happened to you?

25:07.424 --> 25:08.926
What happened there?

25:09.426 --> 25:10.970
Never meet your heroes.

25:12.179 --> 25:13.430
I'll take another.

25:13.764 --> 25:15.391
And that'll be his last one.

25:21.522 --> 25:23.232
To bleak endings.

25:49.758 --> 25:50.759
Alby?

25:53.887 --> 25:55.139
Can you open this?

25:56.807 --> 25:59.517
I know, I'm just getting
a weird feeling.

25:59.518 --> 26:01.853
He's not answering.
- By the way he was drinking,

26:01.854 --> 26:04.148
he's probably passed out
in a pool of his own piss.

26:04.440 --> 26:05.857
He burnt my hand...

26:05.858 --> 26:06.942
Would you just open it!

26:10.446 --> 26:11.822
Your funeral.

26:16.076 --> 26:17.536
Mr Bauman?

26:19.955 --> 26:21.206
It's Fiona.

26:22.374 --> 26:24.168
You left your things in the bar.

26:25.586 --> 26:27.254
Mr Bauman?

26:29.381 --> 26:31.091
Jesus Christ! Alby!

28:32.129 --> 28:34.631
Thanks very much for your time,
Guards.

28:40.304 --> 28:41.388
Mr Bauman...

28:42.014 --> 28:43.390
Are you closing?

28:43.849 --> 28:45.225
End of season.

28:45.934 --> 28:47.728
How, uh...

28:48.854 --> 28:51.315
- How are you feeling?
- I'm sorry.

28:53.066 --> 28:55.861
I just, uh,
came to get my stuff.

28:56.528 --> 28:57.446
Of course.

28:57.821 --> 29:00.449
It's just, uh, back here,
safe and sound.

29:05.537 --> 29:06.872
Thank you.

29:12.419 --> 29:13.837
Hey, uh...

29:14.796 --> 29:16.089
Who found me?

29:17.716 --> 29:21.428
One of, uh,
the members of staff, Fiona.

29:21.762 --> 29:23.513
She was working in the bar
that night.

29:23.514 --> 29:26.141
Christ... Is she around?

29:27.351 --> 29:28.643
No.

29:28.644 --> 29:32.396
Well, I'd like to talk
to her. Apologise.

29:32.397 --> 29:34.149
Could I get her number?

29:34.775 --> 29:38.904
Uh, Mr Bauman, um,
Fiona's missing.

29:39.196 --> 29:40.614
What do you mean?

29:41.782 --> 29:43.950
She hasn't been seen
since Halloween,

29:43.951 --> 29:45.786
and that's weeks ago.

29:46.119 --> 29:47.286
What?

29:50.457 --> 29:53.167
We thought maybe
she just wanted some time

29:53.168 --> 29:55.087
and didn't let
anybody know, but...

29:56.463 --> 29:58.298
What do they think
happened to her?

29:58.465 --> 29:59.758
They don't know.

30:00.300 --> 30:01.634
Well...

30:01.635 --> 30:04.095
Okay, but she couldn't
have just disappeared.

30:04.096 --> 30:07.139
I mean, they searched the hotel?
- Of course.

30:07.140 --> 30:08.475
And the woods.

30:08.809 --> 30:10.352
Could she have been taken?

30:10.686 --> 30:11.728
By who?

30:12.312 --> 30:13.813
Well, how the fuck
should I know?

30:13.814 --> 30:18.818
I mean... local weirdo,
a guest, someone who works here?

30:18.819 --> 30:20.820
I mean, I don't know
if you've noticed

30:20.821 --> 30:23.698
but there are some oddballs
walking around this place.

30:23.699 --> 30:24.866
Okay.

30:26.326 --> 30:29.746
Those men...
they were police.

30:30.163 --> 30:32.081
And there is a man
that they wanna speak with

30:32.082 --> 30:34.084
who lives in the woods.
His name is Jerry.

30:35.210 --> 30:38.714
Fergal saw Fiona outside talking
to him earlier that night.

30:39.423 --> 30:40.799
He hasn't been seen since.

30:42.301 --> 30:46.430
Now, we always just considered
him a pest around here.

30:46.597 --> 30:49.307
He comes into the hotel,
sits by the fire,

30:49.308 --> 30:51.059
bothers the guests.
- Right.

30:52.352 --> 30:54.645
Since his disappearance,

30:54.646 --> 30:57.232
the Guards have learned
who Jerry is, and...

30:58.358 --> 31:02.153
it turns out Jerry disappeared
after his wife died

31:02.154 --> 31:04.406
under suspicious circumstances
ten years ago.

31:07.743 --> 31:10.662
Mr Bauman, I think
you've been through enough.

31:11.371 --> 31:13.456
Go home. Heal.

31:13.457 --> 31:16.209
I promise I'll call you myself
if there's any updates.

31:20.505 --> 31:22.673
I bet you have a whole
new appreciation

31:22.674 --> 31:24.551
for a woman's intuition.

31:26.386 --> 31:28.929
Alby told me that Fiona made him
unlock your door

31:28.930 --> 31:30.891
because she had a bad feeling.

31:31.475 --> 31:32.934
Lucky boy.

31:33.268 --> 31:35.686
You saw Fiona talking
to the man in the woods

31:35.687 --> 31:37.314
before she disappeared?

31:37.481 --> 31:40.692
Jerry. I warned her before
to stay away from him.

31:41.485 --> 31:45.489
Yeah, Mal said his wife died
under suspicious circumstances?

31:46.698 --> 31:48.116
Well, he obviously killed her,
didn't he?

31:49.576 --> 31:52.411
Why else would he be down here
hiding in the woods for years,

31:52.412 --> 31:54.039
living out of an old van.

31:54.706 --> 31:56.540
Oh, well, now he's gone.

31:56.541 --> 31:57.918
He'll be back.

31:59.419 --> 32:00.962
And I'll be waiting for him.

32:02.631 --> 32:04.758
Did you talk to her that night?

32:05.717 --> 32:07.218
- Yeah.
- Yeah?

32:07.219 --> 32:09.221
Wh... How'd she seem?

32:09.596 --> 32:11.181
Well, not herself.

32:12.391 --> 32:13.850
Distracted.

32:14.309 --> 32:15.477
Sad.

32:15.977 --> 32:19.022
I think she was still in shock
from having to cut you down.

32:24.444 --> 32:26.154
Okay, what about
the honeymoon suite?

32:26.947 --> 32:28.073
What about it?

32:28.198 --> 32:30.533
Well, was it searched?

32:30.534 --> 32:32.868
I mean, Fiona mentioned
wanting to go up there.

32:32.869 --> 32:35.079
Impossible.
The gate is always locked.

32:35.080 --> 32:37.290
Mr Cob has the key on him
at all times.

32:38.709 --> 32:40.168
So it wasn't searched?

32:41.253 --> 32:43.422
It's always locked.

32:45.173 --> 32:46.675
It's locked now.

32:47.175 --> 32:49.511
Mr Cob has me
check the gate every day.

32:50.804 --> 32:52.722
There's no way she could have
possibly got up there,

32:52.723 --> 32:55.559
so you might as well suggest
that we search the moon.

32:57.394 --> 32:59.020
Police talk to you?

33:03.066 --> 33:05.026
I talk to the Guards every day.

33:05.902 --> 33:07.487
My first cousins.

33:08.071 --> 33:10.198
Guarda Sergeant is my uncle.

33:11.408 --> 33:12.534
Why do you ask?

33:20.709 --> 33:22.836
See, the best thing
you could do now,

33:24.129 --> 33:25.839
is get into your car

33:25.964 --> 33:27.882
and fuck off back to the airport

33:27.883 --> 33:30.177
while you still look like
your passport picture.

33:37.768 --> 33:39.102
Safe home now.

34:02.125 --> 34:03.376
Come on!

35:01.852 --> 35:04.646
Jesus fucking Christ!

35:04.980 --> 35:07.107
Fiona'd be glad to know
you woke up.

35:07.691 --> 35:09.526
Okay, well, she's missing.

35:12.612 --> 35:14.071
Do you have anything
to do with that?

35:14.072 --> 35:15.156
No.

35:16.908 --> 35:18.409
Well, the police
are looking for you.

35:18.410 --> 35:20.620
You're the last one
seen talking to her.

35:21.329 --> 35:22.705
I don't think it's
the only reason

35:22.706 --> 35:24.249
they're looking for me now.

35:25.000 --> 35:26.084
Huh?

35:26.418 --> 35:28.753
Yeah, that's right.
They said you killed your wife.

35:29.337 --> 35:31.673
Yeah, that's true.

35:33.300 --> 35:35.260
She was very ill.

35:35.927 --> 35:38.305
She was in a lot of pain.

35:40.807 --> 35:42.183
You know...

35:43.393 --> 35:46.103
this is Fiona's.
- We were friends.

35:46.104 --> 35:47.814
She let me borrow it.

35:49.065 --> 35:50.483
Oh, she did?

35:51.109 --> 35:53.903
Okay, well, why don't you
come with me

35:53.904 --> 35:55.988
and we'll talk to the police.

35:55.989 --> 35:57.866
No, it's pointless.

35:57.991 --> 35:59.993
They-they wouldn't
believe me anyway.

36:00.201 --> 36:01.369
Oh yeah?

36:01.494 --> 36:03.121
Why? What do you think
happened to her?

36:03.455 --> 36:04.873
I don't know.

36:05.248 --> 36:06.917
But I know she's dead.

36:09.461 --> 36:11.128
Why do you say that?

36:11.129 --> 36:12.546
There's a cupboard
in Mal's office

36:12.547 --> 36:14.174
full of medicine
left behind by guests.

36:15.258 --> 36:18.178
Two nights ago,
I went there to stock up...

36:19.387 --> 36:21.306
I-I saw her.

37:18.780 --> 37:20.155
What?

37:20.156 --> 37:22.241
And-and the bell
she was pointing to,

37:22.242 --> 37:24.451
it's an old mechanical call bell

37:24.452 --> 37:26.621
connected to the honeymoon
suite.

37:28.623 --> 37:31.584
I think she was trying
to tell me to go up there.

37:34.546 --> 37:36.171
I'm waiting till
the hotel's empty

37:36.172 --> 37:37.465
and then I'm going up there
to check.

37:37.966 --> 37:41.052
Okay, but unless you have a key,
then how the hell...

37:41.970 --> 37:43.762
Ah, right. Of course.

37:43.763 --> 37:46.432
Cob lives on the other side
of the woods. I broke in.

37:46.433 --> 37:49.018
But if he had the key,
then she couldn't be up there.

37:49.019 --> 37:50.936
No, unless someone stole it,

37:50.937 --> 37:53.565
took her up there and then put
it back without him noticing.

37:53.898 --> 37:55.399
Right, but who would do that?

37:55.400 --> 37:56.359
I don't know!

37:58.319 --> 38:00.821
Okay. Why don't you
give it to me?

38:00.822 --> 38:02.740
I'll go back and I'll check.
- No, you-you...

38:02.741 --> 38:04.575
You wouldn't even
get near the gate

38:04.576 --> 38:06.076
with Fergal or Mal still there.

38:06.077 --> 38:07.746
No. It has to be at night.

38:08.121 --> 38:09.330
Tonight...

38:10.123 --> 38:11.958
when the hotel is empty.

38:15.962 --> 38:17.505
Would you come with me?

38:19.549 --> 38:22.343
I don't know what I'm gonna find
when I get up there.

38:23.053 --> 38:25.930
I'd rather not go alone.

38:30.727 --> 38:33.480
You know all these things
do exist?

38:36.858 --> 38:40.361
It is just people
with closed minds can't see 'em.

38:45.909 --> 38:49.412
There's one more car
to pass by my count,

38:49.788 --> 38:51.790
then the hotel is empty.

38:52.582 --> 38:55.418
You really think that was
Fiona's ghost that you saw?

38:56.127 --> 38:57.378
Yeah.

38:57.796 --> 39:01.382
Were you drinking your magic
milk when you saw this ghost?

39:02.425 --> 39:04.219
That's how I saw her.

39:04.594 --> 39:06.554
My mind was open.

39:08.932 --> 39:10.642
What the fuck am I doing here?

39:12.519 --> 39:15.688
My wife's spirit
visited me once on a trip.

39:18.733 --> 39:21.402
She thanked me
for ending her suffering.

39:22.695 --> 39:25.240
Said we'd be together
again someday.

39:30.120 --> 39:31.454
Whatever you say, man.

39:34.249 --> 39:36.960
She said we'd be together again.

39:39.003 --> 39:40.547
Believe what you want.

39:46.469 --> 39:48.428
When we go up there, yeah,

39:48.429 --> 39:50.640
and we find Fiona...

39:51.182 --> 39:52.851
you'll believe it too.

39:53.685 --> 39:55.270
And what if we don't find her?

39:56.437 --> 39:58.648
Does that mean all of this
is just in your head?

40:07.031 --> 40:08.158
Okay.

40:48.907 --> 40:51.326
Hey, she-she was kind
of like this.

40:52.785 --> 40:55.204
- Come on.
- Just getting the crossbow.

40:55.205 --> 40:57.080
What? Don't go get that!
We don't need that!

40:58.208 --> 40:59.459
Shit.

41:17.185 --> 41:18.561
Ugh...

41:40.541 --> 41:42.168
Is there someone there?

42:00.687 --> 42:03.773
- Garda Station?
- Áine? It's Fergal.

42:04.274 --> 42:05.400
I have Jerry.

42:05.525 --> 42:07.109
Tell my cousins
I'm bringing him in.

42:07.110 --> 42:08.568
What do you mean,
'you have him'?

42:08.569 --> 42:10.822
- I have to get on the road.
- What? Fergal, no...

45:24.098 --> 45:25.683
Jesus...

47:28.514 --> 47:29.724
Uh...

47:43.362 --> 47:45.656
It's all right, it's all right.

47:46.115 --> 47:47.617
What are you doing here?

47:47.783 --> 47:49.201
You're asking me?

47:50.453 --> 47:52.829
I got a phone call from Mr Cob
in a panic

47:52.830 --> 47:54.915
saying the honeymoon key
was missing.

48:00.963 --> 48:02.631
How'd you even get this?

48:02.632 --> 48:04.467
- Jerry?
- Jerry.

48:04.717 --> 48:06.969
Yeah, he's convinced
Fiona was up here.

48:08.262 --> 48:10.056
Where is he?

48:10.514 --> 48:12.724
Fergal, the fuckhead,
took him to the police.

48:12.725 --> 48:14.060
He didn't see me.

48:15.478 --> 48:16.854
What were you thinking?

48:18.105 --> 48:20.482
Uh, she saved me.
I wanted to help find her.

48:20.483 --> 48:21.484
I don't know.

48:23.653 --> 48:24.987
Okay.

48:25.154 --> 48:27.782
Why don't we just go downstairs?

48:27.907 --> 48:29.574
We'll get in trouble
if we're caught up here.

48:29.575 --> 48:30.660
Alright.

48:31.952 --> 48:34.037
Can you gimme a ride
back to my car?

48:34.038 --> 48:35.039
Yeah.

48:42.171 --> 48:44.215
You're lucky
you didn't get locked in here.

48:44.340 --> 48:46.758
Mr Cob told me a story
about a young bride

48:46.759 --> 48:48.219
locking herself in here once.

48:50.971 --> 48:52.597
Oh no, Mr Bauman...

48:52.598 --> 48:54.433
Mr Bauman, would you please?

48:54.600 --> 48:56.602
You're not supposed
to be up here!

48:56.852 --> 49:00.106
Mr Cob is very strict
on people not coming up here!

49:00.314 --> 49:01.856
I could lose my job!

49:01.857 --> 49:03.275
Where does this go?

49:04.193 --> 49:07.112
There was a basement down there
before it was a hotel.

49:07.113 --> 49:08.029
Uh-huh.

49:08.030 --> 49:08.905
The entrance was lost

49:08.906 --> 49:09.906
during the renovations.

49:09.907 --> 49:11.158
There's nothing down there.

49:13.744 --> 49:14.870
Oh, look at that.

49:16.414 --> 49:18.749
There is nothing down there.

49:27.299 --> 49:30.678
No! Okay, okay.
We need to move, move.

49:30.970 --> 49:32.430
We need to leave!

49:34.765 --> 49:38.435
Mr Bauman, I am going to have
you arrested for trespassing

49:38.436 --> 49:39.936
if you do not leave
right this minute!

49:55.244 --> 49:56.203
Oh...

50:13.846 --> 50:15.848
Hey!

50:29.945 --> 50:31.530
Hey!

50:33.032 --> 50:34.200
Hey!

51:14.406 --> 51:16.283
Idea for a character.

51:17.368 --> 51:20.830
Uh, oblivious charisma vacuum.

51:22.623 --> 51:25.835
Completely incapable
of reading a room.

51:33.467 --> 51:34.677
Hi, girls.

51:35.344 --> 51:36.720
Looking well.

51:40.474 --> 51:42.184
I thought you were gonna
hand that in to the hospital.

51:46.897 --> 51:49.066
He's, uh, famous, you know?

51:49.400 --> 51:51.819
I bet you he'll dedicate his new
book to you if he wakes up.

51:51.944 --> 51:53.779
Don't say 'if', Mal.

51:58.701 --> 52:00.578
Drink your tea
while it's still hot.

52:19.555 --> 52:21.390
- Uh...
- You all right?

52:23.183 --> 52:24.518
I feel...

52:25.811 --> 52:27.104
I feel off.

53:03.223 --> 53:05.017
I'm grateful for it, you know,
it looks awesome.

53:08.854 --> 53:10.521
I can't see a thing
in it, man.

53:10.522 --> 53:12.024
It's absolutely sweating...

53:24.662 --> 53:26.580
It's alright.

53:31.502 --> 53:32.586
Ah...

54:20.634 --> 54:22.469
I know I'm gonna be okay.

54:24.013 --> 54:26.515
I'm gonna leave this message
here just in case.

54:29.977 --> 54:31.854
My name is Fiona Crotty.

54:33.814 --> 54:36.817
I think I'm in the basement
of the hotel, but...

54:37.151 --> 54:38.402
I don't know.

54:44.825 --> 54:46.326
I'm pregnant.

54:49.705 --> 54:52.916
Mal, the manager,
is the father.

54:54.668 --> 54:57.004
He wasn't happy with me
for keeping the baby.

55:03.010 --> 55:05.179
I wasn't gonna tell anyone
it was his,

55:08.390 --> 55:10.433
but he was just so terrified

55:10.434 --> 55:13.812
his wife or father-in-law,
Mr Cob, would find out.

55:15.731 --> 55:18.233
I can't believe
he'd go this far.

55:18.901 --> 55:20.527
Put us down here.

55:21.153 --> 55:22.571
Get rid of us.

55:28.410 --> 55:30.119
It's dark,

55:30.120 --> 55:33.040
but I'm gonna see
if I can find a way out.

55:33.707 --> 55:37.336
If I don't and someone
finds this message,

55:38.796 --> 55:40.464
tell my parents I love them.

57:07.551 --> 57:09.094
Fuckin' Fergal...

57:41.877 --> 57:42.961
Shit...

58:14.368 --> 58:15.911
No, no, no, no, no, no.

58:20.040 --> 58:21.124
Fuck!

58:21.416 --> 58:22.709
Fuck!

59:26.440 --> 59:27.733
Hello?

01:00:31.004 --> 01:00:31.963
Hey!

01:00:32.214 --> 01:00:33.340
Who's there?

01:01:11.461 --> 01:01:13.337
Aargh!

01:01:14.756 --> 01:01:19.844
Okay, kids, we're gonna read
our next letter!

01:01:19.845 --> 01:01:21.763
Yay!

01:01:22.097 --> 01:01:24.516
"Dear Jack..."
That's me!

01:01:24.891 --> 01:01:27.601
"My name is Ohm Bauman."

01:01:27.602 --> 01:01:28.937
Ohm? Okay.

01:01:29.688 --> 01:01:33.817
"I am ten years old
and my mom died last year."

01:01:34.568 --> 01:01:37.820
- What dies, kids?
- Everything!

01:01:37.821 --> 01:01:41.867
"I was playing with my dad's
gun and it went off."

01:01:42.451 --> 01:01:46.620
What are the two things
we don't ever play with, kids?

01:01:46.621 --> 01:01:48.289
- Fire!
- And?

01:01:48.290 --> 01:01:50.584
- Guns!
- That's right!

01:01:51.251 --> 01:01:53.503
"My dad hates me now."

01:01:53.712 --> 01:01:55.379
"I miss my mom."

01:01:55.380 --> 01:01:57.591
"I'm scared all the time."

01:01:57.716 --> 01:02:00.051
"Can you help me? Ohm."

01:02:00.886 --> 01:02:03.846
Well, Ohm, it's pretty simple.

01:02:03.847 --> 01:02:06.807
Your dad told you
not to go near his gun,

01:02:06.808 --> 01:02:08.934
but you did anyway.

01:02:08.935 --> 01:02:12.771
And his wife got her brains
blown out.

01:02:14.483 --> 01:02:17.151
You want help?
There's none coming.

01:02:17.152 --> 01:02:19.612
You're scared? You should be.

01:02:19.613 --> 01:02:21.864
You fucking should be!

01:03:36.523 --> 01:03:38.149
There's no way back up.

01:03:38.858 --> 01:03:40.944
The dumbwaiter button's broken.

01:03:42.320 --> 01:03:44.406
I can't use it to get back up.

01:03:46.783 --> 01:03:48.660
I can't find a way out.

01:03:51.246 --> 01:03:53.081
I'm stuck down here.

01:04:29.534 --> 01:04:30.744
Yes!

01:05:03.401 --> 01:05:04.444
Right...

01:05:59.833 --> 01:06:01.543
Oh! Ah...

01:06:03.628 --> 01:06:05.380
Oh, fuckin' Jesus.

01:06:21.479 --> 01:06:22.647
Ah...

01:09:08.521 --> 01:09:10.565
I think there's someone
down here!

01:09:12.984 --> 01:09:14.861
I keep hearing something.

01:09:21.659 --> 01:09:23.202
Is someone there?

01:09:25.622 --> 01:09:28.124
Oh God! Oh...

01:10:35.525 --> 01:10:37.986
Three, two...

01:10:48.246 --> 01:10:49.872
Come on! Come on...

01:10:51.624 --> 01:10:52.792
Come on...

01:10:58.297 --> 01:10:59.674
Hello?

01:12:56.040 --> 01:12:57.416
Aah...

01:15:35.616 --> 01:15:36.701
Uh...

01:15:37.493 --> 01:15:38.911
- Jesus...
- Ah, Mal.

01:15:39.412 --> 01:15:40.870
I need your help.

01:15:40.871 --> 01:15:43.624
Jesus, Jerry.
What happened to you?

01:15:43.916 --> 01:15:46.543
Oh, Fergal. It doesn't matter.

01:15:46.544 --> 01:15:47.794
I need to get up here.

01:15:47.795 --> 01:15:49.170
I need to get this open.

01:15:49.171 --> 01:15:50.880
- What for?
- The American.

01:15:50.881 --> 01:15:52.675
Ohm, he went up there.

01:15:53.301 --> 01:15:55.636
- Ugh!
- Stop! Stop, stop.

01:15:56.429 --> 01:15:57.638
He's gone.

01:15:58.222 --> 01:15:59.514
What?

01:15:59.515 --> 01:16:02.559
Mr Cob sent me out here
to look for the key,

01:16:02.560 --> 01:16:04.144
and when I got here,
the gate was unlocked,

01:16:04.145 --> 01:16:05.938
so I went up.
- And?

01:16:07.023 --> 01:16:09.233
- What did you find?
- Mr Bauman.

01:16:09.358 --> 01:16:11.986
- Drunk.
- What?

01:16:12.361 --> 01:16:15.363
- Where is he?
- He's on his way to the airport.

01:16:15.364 --> 01:16:17.991
Well, he was too drunk to drive,
so I took him down to town,

01:16:17.992 --> 01:16:19.952
stuffed him in a taxi
and sent him off.

01:16:20.161 --> 01:16:21.829
And Fiona?

01:16:23.122 --> 01:16:24.332
No.

01:17:28.562 --> 01:17:29.772
Hey...

01:17:33.859 --> 01:17:35.528
So, you just jumped?

01:17:36.570 --> 01:17:38.197
I mean, you could
have been killed.

01:17:44.328 --> 01:17:45.995
Are you sure
you checked that room?

01:17:45.996 --> 01:17:47.747
I mean, you looked everywhere?

01:17:47.748 --> 01:17:49.416
The room's not that big.

01:17:49.417 --> 01:17:52.545
She's not there.
I swear to you, I looked.

01:17:52.920 --> 01:17:54.755
I need to see it for myself.

01:17:56.215 --> 01:17:58.300
Fiona wants me to go up there.

01:17:58.426 --> 01:18:01.136
I'm going to have to call
the guards

01:18:01.137 --> 01:18:02.763
to tell them you're here.

01:18:06.642 --> 01:18:08.602
They know about your wife.

01:18:12.440 --> 01:18:13.691
I saw her...

01:18:14.733 --> 01:18:16.110
I saw her.

01:18:17.945 --> 01:18:19.864
Just go, Jerry.

01:18:20.406 --> 01:18:23.784
Take Bauman's car
and don't come back.

01:18:24.618 --> 01:18:26.662
I'll tell them
that you were already gone.

01:18:29.206 --> 01:18:30.624
Just go.

01:19:53.707 --> 01:19:55.291
No, no, no! Jerry!

01:19:55.292 --> 01:19:56.418
Jerry!

01:20:19.483 --> 01:20:20.484
Jerry!

01:20:20.859 --> 01:20:22.027
Jerry!

01:20:27.116 --> 01:20:28.242
Aah...

01:20:50.848 --> 01:20:52.182
Uh!

01:20:52.600 --> 01:20:53.726
Ah!

01:20:57.187 --> 01:20:58.564
I left the keys.

01:21:04.153 --> 01:21:05.779
Motherfucker...

01:21:09.450 --> 01:21:10.868
Are you all right, Mal?

01:21:11.285 --> 01:21:14.079
No, I'm-I'm actually
not feeling the best.

01:21:15.080 --> 01:21:18.375
I think I might need to lock up
and go home.

01:21:18.876 --> 01:21:20.961
Hey, why don't I get the keys
and I'll bring them out to you?

01:22:07.383 --> 01:22:09.468
God damn it!

01:22:38.872 --> 01:22:44.962
♪ Oft, in the stilly night ♪

01:22:45.295 --> 01:22:51.552
♪ Ere slumber's chain
has bound me ♪

01:22:53.470 --> 01:22:59.560
♪ Fond memory
brings the light ♪

01:23:00.978 --> 01:23:03.522
- Jerry.
- Fiona used to say,

01:23:04.565 --> 01:23:07.276
never ignore when something
feels off.

01:23:11.196 --> 01:23:13.282
Something feels off here, Mal.

01:23:13.449 --> 01:23:14.491
Jerry...

01:23:15.701 --> 01:23:16.784
You have to leave.

01:23:16.785 --> 01:23:18.453
If you dropped Ohm into town,

01:23:18.454 --> 01:23:20.247
why did you come back out here?

01:23:23.333 --> 01:23:26.295
To get this...
reframed for my wife.

01:23:28.422 --> 01:23:30.632
You drove all the way back out
here for that?

01:23:30.966 --> 01:23:32.717
Can't a man do something
nice for his wife

01:23:32.718 --> 01:23:33.968
without having
something to hide?

01:23:47.775 --> 01:23:49.526
- Uh...
- Jerry...

01:23:49.777 --> 01:23:51.319
Jerry, what the fuck
are you doing?

01:23:51.320 --> 01:23:53.154
- Key!
- I don't have it.

01:23:53.155 --> 01:23:54.572
I gave it back to Mr Cob.

01:23:54.573 --> 01:23:55.783
Give it to me!

01:23:56.366 --> 01:23:59.119
Okay. Okay, okay.

01:24:04.625 --> 01:24:06.335
Jerry, please.

01:24:06.585 --> 01:24:08.045
It was a mistake.

01:24:08.170 --> 01:24:09.754
You don't know Fiona like I did.

01:24:09.755 --> 01:24:11.214
She wasn't a good person!

01:24:11.215 --> 01:24:13.300
You know, she was threatening
to tell Mr Cob!

01:24:13.884 --> 01:24:15.676
And he hates me!

01:24:15.677 --> 01:24:18.472
He's threatened to have me
killed for less over the years!

01:24:19.223 --> 01:24:20.515
Just leave him!

01:24:20.516 --> 01:24:22.642
He was gonna
kill himself anyway!

01:24:31.985 --> 01:24:37.366
♪ I've seen
around me fall ♪

01:24:38.158 --> 01:24:44.706
♪ Like leaves
in wintry weather ♪

01:24:45.707 --> 01:24:48.710
♪ I feel like one ♪

01:24:49.294 --> 01:24:52.047
♪ Who treads alone ♪

01:24:52.631 --> 01:24:58.804
♪ Some banquet-hall deserted ♪

01:25:05.269 --> 01:25:08.146
- Ohm!
- Hey! Jerry!

01:25:08.605 --> 01:25:11.315
I'm in here! Get me
the fuck out of here, man!

01:25:18.991 --> 01:25:20.576
There's a small door here!

01:25:21.702 --> 01:25:23.287
I can bust it open.

01:25:24.037 --> 01:25:25.372
Yeah.

01:25:25.497 --> 01:25:26.874
Stay back, stay back.

01:25:28.709 --> 01:25:30.043
Uh!

01:25:35.132 --> 01:25:36.674
- Fiona?
- No, she's dead.

01:25:36.675 --> 01:25:38.302
Mal fucking killed her.

01:25:40.470 --> 01:25:41.597
Are you okay?

01:25:42.764 --> 01:25:44.307
I'll live.

01:25:44.308 --> 01:25:45.434
Uh!

01:26:03.160 --> 01:26:05.370
Don't try and leave!

01:26:05.746 --> 01:26:07.080
I mean it!

01:26:27.684 --> 01:26:29.978
Oh, fuck!

01:26:30.520 --> 01:26:31.897
Aaargh!

01:26:33.357 --> 01:26:35.317
God! Fuck!

01:27:12.437 --> 01:27:13.730
Bauman?

01:27:17.985 --> 01:27:19.236
Fuck...

01:27:22.572 --> 01:27:23.824
Bauman!

01:27:48.348 --> 01:27:50.017
Bauman, listen to me.

01:27:50.600 --> 01:27:52.309
The hotel is on fire.

01:27:52.310 --> 01:27:54.354
There's no way out down there.

01:27:54.688 --> 01:27:56.814
I'll bring you back up
with the key

01:27:56.815 --> 01:27:58.316
and we can both leave.

01:27:58.442 --> 01:28:00.068
You can go home.

01:28:01.069 --> 01:28:02.154
Bauman!

01:28:02.821 --> 01:28:04.239
Can you hear me?

01:28:20.881 --> 01:28:22.132
Ohm...

01:28:48.992 --> 01:28:50.327
Bauman?

01:30:09.447 --> 01:30:10.866
Ah!

01:30:12.492 --> 01:30:13.702
Uh!

01:31:06.922 --> 01:31:08.882
It was an accident.

01:31:12.427 --> 01:31:16.097
I'm sorry, it was an accident.

01:31:16.431 --> 01:31:17.724
I know.

01:31:21.144 --> 01:31:22.938
You can't stay here.

01:31:28.610 --> 01:31:30.612
It was an accident.

01:31:58.181 --> 01:31:59.516
What's happening?

01:32:20.870 --> 01:32:21.955
Help!

01:32:28.044 --> 01:32:29.296
Please! No!

01:32:38.638 --> 01:32:40.223
Aaaargh!

01:34:52.147 --> 01:34:53.356
Mal!

01:34:56.901 --> 01:34:58.027
Mal!

01:34:59.946 --> 01:35:00.947
Mal!

01:35:01.948 --> 01:35:03.366
Can you hear me?

01:35:05.410 --> 01:35:06.744
Ohm's Mum: Fergal!

01:35:08.830 --> 01:35:10.457
Is there someone there?

01:35:16.754 --> 01:35:18.173
Jesus...

01:35:18.965 --> 01:35:20.550
Hey! Hey, hey, hey!

01:35:21.050 --> 01:35:22.927
Come on, we have to go! Up!

01:35:27.265 --> 01:35:28.975
Come on! We have to go!

01:35:48.411 --> 01:35:50.413
How are you feeling, Mr Bauman?

01:35:55.376 --> 01:35:56.628
You're that bellboy.

01:35:57.545 --> 01:35:58.838
My name's Alby.

01:35:59.672 --> 01:36:01.215
I didn't think you'd have
anybody visiting you,

01:36:01.216 --> 01:36:02.467
being away from home.

01:36:02.800 --> 01:36:05.345
I'm not sure I'd have anybody
visiting me there either.

01:36:08.139 --> 01:36:09.598
Sit down, sorry.

01:36:14.562 --> 01:36:17.774
Okay. Uh, I guess I'll just get
two scoops of vanilla.

01:36:18.233 --> 01:36:22.152
Yeah, I work in the ice cream
parlour next door as well, yeah.

01:36:22.153 --> 01:36:23.279
Ah.

01:36:23.696 --> 01:36:25.573
Oh, this is from Fergal.

01:36:27.992 --> 01:36:30.161
He's pretty devastated
about Fiona.

01:36:30.411 --> 01:36:32.204
He said if you needed anything
to let him know.

01:36:32.205 --> 01:36:33.790
Yeah, I spoke to him
on the phone.

01:36:34.040 --> 01:36:34.999
Oh.

01:36:36.251 --> 01:36:37.835
You been to the hotel?

01:36:38.044 --> 01:36:39.420
What's left of it.

01:36:40.880 --> 01:36:42.382
They found remains.

01:36:42.966 --> 01:36:44.592
Fiona and Jerry.

01:36:47.804 --> 01:36:49.013
Mal?

01:36:49.180 --> 01:36:50.974
His car was found outside.

01:36:51.224 --> 01:36:52.767
They're looking for him.

01:36:57.480 --> 01:37:00.900
Mr Bauman, I need
to tell you something.

01:37:03.695 --> 01:37:06.197
I don't what happened, um,

01:37:06.573 --> 01:37:09.492
but I'm worried it might have
been my fault in some way.

01:37:10.660 --> 01:37:11.786
How?

01:37:12.912 --> 01:37:15.248
There was a flask of whiskey
in your room.

01:37:16.374 --> 01:37:18.710
- Did you drink it?
- Yeah.

01:37:19.210 --> 01:37:20.503
Much of it?

01:37:20.878 --> 01:37:23.631
Well, it's whiskey.
I drink all of it. Why?

01:37:25.258 --> 01:37:26.759
I spiked it.

01:37:28.177 --> 01:37:29.679
With what?

01:37:30.388 --> 01:37:32.765
I had some of Jerry's
mushroom powder.

01:37:33.057 --> 01:37:36.102
I snuck into your room
and I put it in the flask.

01:37:38.187 --> 01:37:39.731
Why would you do that?

01:37:40.064 --> 01:37:41.607
Well, it was after
I tried to speak to you

01:37:41.608 --> 01:37:42.942
at the bar that night.

01:37:44.110 --> 01:37:45.777
You burnt my hand.

01:37:45.778 --> 01:37:47.155
That hurt.

01:37:50.533 --> 01:37:53.244
You know, all these
things do exist.

01:37:53.620 --> 01:37:57.332
It's just people with closed
minds can't see 'em.

01:38:01.794 --> 01:38:03.129
I'm sorry.

01:38:04.047 --> 01:38:05.882
You were really rude.

01:38:08.426 --> 01:38:10.470
I'd better go
before they kick me out.

01:38:10.970 --> 01:38:13.890
One of the firemen
found this at the hotel.

01:38:22.940 --> 01:38:24.567
Hey, um...

01:38:25.985 --> 01:38:27.487
you can take that, too.

01:38:28.279 --> 01:38:29.613
I didn't touch it.

01:38:29.614 --> 01:38:31.282
Yeah, no, just, just take it.

01:38:35.787 --> 01:38:37.829
If you wanted something
to pass the time,

01:38:37.830 --> 01:38:38.956
I could bring in my manuscript.

01:38:41.334 --> 01:38:43.586
I mean, I've been
through enough already, Alby.

01:38:46.464 --> 01:38:48.508
I'll do a quick polish tonight
and drop it in tomorrow.

01:38:49.550 --> 01:38:50.593
All right.

01:39:34.929 --> 01:39:36.848
I said turn away!

01:39:54.657 --> 01:39:55.950
Aaargh!

01:40:07.336 --> 01:40:08.463
Here.

01:40:09.589 --> 01:40:11.007
Hit me here.

01:40:12.633 --> 01:40:15.595
As hard as you can.
You understand?

01:40:17.388 --> 01:40:18.973
You don't stop for blood.

01:40:19.098 --> 01:40:20.307
You don't stop for bone

01:40:20.308 --> 01:40:23.019
and you keep hitting
until it breaks.

01:40:25.188 --> 01:40:27.732
Follows the map and you claim it
all as yours.

01:40:31.444 --> 01:40:33.404
It's nothing I don't deserve.

01:40:39.827 --> 01:40:41.621
Do it before I change my mind.

01:40:43.122 --> 01:40:44.081
No.

01:40:44.207 --> 01:40:45.291
No...

01:42:16.716 --> 01:42:21.303
♪ Farewell vain world
I'm going home ♪

01:42:21.304 --> 01:42:25.099
♪ My saviour smiles
and bids me come ♪

01:42:25.266 --> 01:42:28.561
♪ And I don't care
to stay here long ♪

01:42:28.769 --> 01:42:33.107
♪ Sweet angels
beckon me away ♪

01:42:33.232 --> 01:42:36.944
♪ To sing God's praise
in endless day ♪

01:42:37.153 --> 01:42:40.448
♪ And I don't care
to stay here long ♪

01:42:40.573 --> 01:42:43.533
♪ Right up yonder ♪

01:42:43.534 --> 01:42:47.079
♪ Christians away up yonder ♪

01:42:47.330 --> 01:42:49.789
♪ Oh yes, my Lord ♪

01:42:49.790 --> 01:42:53.502
♪ For I don't care
to stay here long ♪

01:42:54.086 --> 01:42:58.424
♪ I'm glad that I am
born to die ♪

01:42:58.549 --> 01:43:02.303
♪ From grief and woe
my soul shall fly ♪

01:43:02.470 --> 01:43:05.681
♪ And I don't care
to stay here long ♪

01:43:05.890 --> 01:43:10.102
♪ Bright angels
shall convey me home ♪

01:43:10.269 --> 01:43:13.940
♪ Away to New Jerusalem ♪

01:43:14.148 --> 01:43:17.318
♪ And I don't care
to stay here long ♪

01:43:17.526 --> 01:43:20.404
♪ Right up yonder ♪

01:43:20.529 --> 01:43:23.866
♪ Christians away up yonder ♪

01:43:24.200 --> 01:43:26.660
♪ Oh yes, my Lord ♪

01:43:26.661 --> 01:43:29.830
♪ For I don't care
to stay here long ♪

01:43:30.039 --> 01:43:32.917
♪ Right up yonder ♪

01:43:33.042 --> 01:43:36.504
♪ Christians away up yonder ♪

01:43:36.629 --> 01:43:39.048
♪ Oh yes, my Lord ♪

01:43:39.173 --> 01:43:43.427
♪ For I don't care
